Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 14:16:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 042/154] feat: delete the ABI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

atrium_bridge.h, atrium_ui_bridge.h and atrium_ui_bridge.mm are gone: 3,699
lines of frozen vtable, export declarations and the dlopen loader that
resolved 63 symbols into nil-checked groups so a missing dylib degraded to
vanilla Chromium. A statically linked crate cannot be absent, so every
degraded branch was dead the day Swift was deleted.

Seventeen files lose their include. Nothing calls dlopen for Atrium any more.

AtriumHost is retired rather than replaced. It was an opaque handle Swift
used to name a window, and its definition was
`reinterpret_cast<AtriumHost*>(this)` - the controller's own address wearing
a different type. With no ABI to hide the type from, it collapses to the
BrowserController* it always was, and ControllerFor keeps validating against
the live registry, which is the part that was ever load-bearing.

The comments that cite the header's doc blocks by name keep the names -
SIDEBAR WIDTH, SPLIT VIEW, EDIT FOCUS, TAB CYCLING. Those blocks are the
semantics of each op rather than its signature, and are worth reading before
rebuilding one. docs/host-ops-inventory.md says how to get them back.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn                              | 3 ---
 chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc                            | 1 -
 chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_window_factory.cc | 1 -
 3 files changed, 5 deletions(-)

